From 9679c54bf300a93d122dbc52c49bbe0eeb725a25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:53:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 48/51] wifi: ath12k: do not tell peach the QDSS config is
 missing

With CNSS_QDSS_CFG_MISS in the host feature list, peach starts
initializing before the host has sent aux_ucode20.elf and the QDSS
trace config: both are refused with QMI error 90 (incompatible
state) and the firmware asserts in whal_aux_mac_trigger_wakeup.
Stock cnss2 sets the bit only when the QDSS file is missing, and
ROCKNIX's WCN7860 port (same PCI id) drops it for the same crash.
Without it (feature list 0x50) aux and QDSS are accepted and the
firmware reaches WMI ready; wlan0 registers.

7.3 port: 7.3 sends hw_params->qmi_cnss_feature_bitmap as the host
feature list, so the bit is dropped from the WCN7860 entry (cloned
from QCC2072) instead of being masked in host_cap_send.

(reworked from commit 0b2e2875c)
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
index 4736a0feb..095a0bc1e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -863,8 +863,12 @@ static const struct ath12k_hw_params ath12k_wifi7_hw_params[] = {
 
 		.wmi_init = ath12k_wifi7_wmi_init_wcn7850,
 
-		.qmi_cnss_feature_bitmap = BIT(CNSS_QDSS_CFG_MISS_V01) |
-					   BIT(CNSS_PCIE_PERST_NO_PULL_V01) |
+		/* Not QDSS_CFG_MISS: with it peach starts initializing at
+		 * once, rejects aux and qdss with err 90 (incompatible
+		 * state) and asserts in the aux MAC wakeup. Stock cnss2 sets
+		 * it only when the qdss file is missing. 0x50.
+		 */
+		.qmi_cnss_feature_bitmap = BIT(CNSS_PCIE_PERST_NO_PULL_V01) |
 					   BIT(CNSS_AUX_UC_SUPPORT_V01),
 
 		.rfkill_pin = 0,
-- 
